1-; =============================================================================
2-; Vexa Lite (v0.12) — single-container process supervisor
3-; =============================================================================
4-; Runs the v0.12 control plane in ONE container: the four long-running Python services
5:; (admin-api · runtime · meeting-api · gateway) + the agent control plane (agent-api) +
6-; over an internal redis + a shared Xvfb/PulseAudio audio-video stack.
7-;
8-; The bot and the agent WORKER are NOT supervised here: the runtime (RUNTIME_BACKEND=process)
9-; spawns them as CHILD PROCESSES on demand via the in-container launchers
10-; (BOT_COMMAND / AGENT_WORKER_COMMAND — defaulted by the entrypoint to the /usr/local/bin
11-; launchers, interpolated here via %(ENV_…)s so operator-provided container env wins),
12-; sharing this container's display/audio — the lite analog of compose's docker-socket spawn.
13-; =============================================================================
14-[supervisord]
15-nodaemon=true
16-logfile=/var/log/supervisor/supervisord.log
17-pidfile=/var/run/supervisord.pid
18-childlogdir=/var/log/supervisor
19-logfile_maxbytes=50MB
20-logfile_backups=3
21-loglevel=info
